Finnish is like this. It does use verbal emphasis, but unlike English, which
has strict word order rules, Finnish puts endings on words and allows more
flexible word ordering. (I would say, as a non-native speaker, that the
default is the English-like subject-verb-object).

For instance:

Sinä = you
kadotit = lost
sen = it

*You* lost it.
Sinähän kadotit sen. (-hän or -han is an emphasis ending)

You *lost* it.
Kadotit sinä sen.

You lost it.
Se kadotit sinä.

I've noticed some Finnish names in the newsgroup; perhaps someone can
